Afterwards Mr. Qi rushes at the player, causing the player to pass out and wake up in Harvey's Clinic. Further attempts result in the player passing out immediately after entering the map.

Treehouse - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Treehouse is home to Leo after he moves to the mainland from Ginger Island. It's located on the Mountain, in a large tree east of the entrance of the Railroad and west of Linus' tent.

Before Leo moves to the mainland, it is just a large tree. The night after the player reaches 6 hearts with Leo and he agrees to move to the mainland, a cutscene will show the parrots transforming the tree into Leo's treehouse.

Elliott's Cabin - General: {{Infobox location

}}
Elliott's Cabin is the home of Elliott. It's located directly east when entering The Beach.

During Spring, Summer, and Fall, players must first acquire two hearts of friendship with Elliott before being allowed inside his cabin. Players at any friendship level may enter during Winter between 10am and 6pm.

Fish Shop - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Fish Shop is the home of Saturdays, the shop will be closed unless it is raining, with the exception of Winter 13, the second day of SquidFest.

Willy sells a variety of rods, fish tanks, and crab pots. Some items, such as tackles, become available once the player reaches a specific fishing level. Those items can be purchased as soon as the appropriate skill level is achieved, without needing to wait until the next day. Other items, such as the Copper Pan and the Deluxe Fish Tank, require the player to complete specific tasks to become available.

The shop is closed on all festival days, with exception of Desert Festival, Trout Derby, SquidFest and Night Market, as well as Spirit's Eve.

Oasis - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Oasis is a store located in The Desert and run by Sandy, open from 9am to 11:50pm. It sells unique seeds as well as items purchasable from other shops, sometimes at a reduced price.

The path in the back leads to the "The Mysterious Qi" quest.

The festival days with the exception of the Desert Festival.

Island Field Office - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Island Field Office can be found in Volcano and east of the Dig Site.

Until Professor Snail is rescued from the nearby cave, the office remains empty with no interactable elements. After the rescue, donate fossils at the office work desk or answer the Island Surveys posted on the wall to receive Golden Walnuts.

Island Trader - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Island Trader is a bluebird merchant located on the North side of Ginger Island. Like the Desert Trader, the Island Trader does not accept gold but only barters in exchange for other items.

The Island Trader is unlocked for Golden Walnuts after purchasing the Island Farmhouse.

Qi's Walnut Room - General: {{Infobox location

}}
The Walnut Room is located on the West side of Ginger Island. It can be opened once the player obtains a total of 100 golden walnuts (see Note below). Inside is a Perfection Tracker, a Special Order Board, and a Vending Machine that sells items in exchange for Qi Gems.

Qi Gems can't be earned before unlocking the room, as the 3 methods to obtain them (via the Special Orders Board, by activating the Shrine of Challenge, and by exchanging Golden Walnuts) require entering this room.

Cabin-- General - {{Infobox building

}}
:For cabin placement, see Cabin Locations
:For cabin/farmhouse storage, see Keg
The Cabin is a farm building that enables the ability to house one farmhand each in a Multiplayer game.

They behave much like the Farmhouse, but belong to a farmhand rather than the host of the game. Up to 7 cabins can be present on computer and Nintendo Switch 2, and up to 3 on other consoles. They may be chosen at the start of a new co-op game, in "Nearby" or "Separate" layout, or can also be added to a saved game by visiting the Carpenter's Shop and choosing "Construct farm buildings" from the menu. If chosen at the start of a Multiplayer game, cabins are free. If built on an existing farm, the cost is for each of the 7 varieties of Cabin. Cabins are built instantaneously upon purchase.

Greenhouse - General: {{Infobox building

}}

The Greenhouse is a building present on the farm from the start. It is initially in a state of disrepair, making it unusable. It can be repaired by completing the Pantry Bundles for the Community Center or by purchasing "Greenhouse" from the Joja Community Development Form for . Once repaired, it can be moved by talking to Robin at the Carpenter's Shop.

On the Standard Farm Map, moving the Greenhouse causes the decorative grass beneath it to disappear permanently, making it impossible to undo the action or restore the grass.

Mill - General: {{Infobox building

}}
The Mill is a farm building purchasable from Robin at the Carpenter's Shop. It takes two days for Robin to complete its construction.

Pet Bowl - General: {{Infobox building

}}
The Pet Bowl is a farm building purchasable from pet. This free Pet Bowl remains on the farm, even if the player declines to adopt the pet.

Additional Pet Bowls do not have to be constructed before adopting more pets from friendship points the next morning.

Silo - General: {{Infobox building

}}

The Silo is a type of farm building purchasable from Robin at the Carpenter's Shop. It takes two days to build. When complete, it stores hay from grass cut on the farm.

Slime Hutch - General: {{Infobox building

}}
The Slime Hutch is a farm building purchasable from Robin at the Carpenter's Shop that stores up to 20 Slimes.

Stable - General: {{Infobox building

}}
The Stable is a farm building purchasable from horse, which is included with the stable. The horse will be found in the stable at the start of each day.

After the stable is built, the player is able to name the horse the first time it is ridden.

A farm can normally have only one stable, but in multiplayer games, each player can build their own stable.

Well - General: {{Infobox building

}}

The Well is a farm building purchasable from Watering Can. It takes two days for Robin to complete its construction.

Gold Clock - General: {{Infobox building

}}
The Gold Clock is a type of building purchasable from the Goblin Problem".

After placing the Gold Clock, it can be turned on or off.

Constructing the Gold Clock is necessary to achieve Perfection.

Junimo Hut - General: {{Infobox building

}}

The Junimo Hut is a type of building purchasable from the Goblin Problem Quest, and returning the bottle of ink from the witches hut to the wizard.

The hut houses Junimos, who live on the player's farm and harvest fully-grown crops that are within the hut's vicinity.

